* Support --and-widget chaining. This requires a different execution
  model: one dialog process displays several widgets, and the output of
  each widget is separated with --separate-widget. Pythondialog
  currently runs one process per widget.

* Support the output-affecting options --output-separator (and its
  --separator alias), --quoted, --single-quoted, --no-items and
  --last-key. They are understood by dialog, but exposing them as common
  options without extending every output parser would silently corrupt
  widget return values.

* Add convenience methods for --print-text-only and --print-text-size.

* Check for terminal resizing?..
